# MendWise — project rules

Wound-assessment app grounded in two clinical guides (Australian Govt CWCS + Mölnlycke).
Full context: `docs/MendWise_Assessment_Build_Spec.md`; current state + next task: `docs/HANDOFF.md`.
Read both before non-trivial work. This is a **research prototype — not a medical device**.

## The cage (do not violate)
- **Determinism is authoritative.** The dressing/referral decision comes ONLY from the deterministic engine in `src/decision/engine.ts` (CWCS 26-pathway table + Mölnlycke triggers). AI never emits a pathway.
- **AI is caged.** SAM 2 = boundary only; OpenCV HSI = tissue % only; frontier VLM = strict-JSON enums only (`generateObject` + Zod, `temperature: 0`); frontier LLM = narrate already-decided facts only.
- **Additive, never destructive.** New work goes behind an `assessmentV2` flag + `/api/v1/assessments/*`; keep the existing capture→analyze→questions→result flow working.
- **Conservative by default.** No marker / low confidence / conflicting signals → "incomplete → retake or escalate".
- **No model fine-tuning.** Zero-shot models only.

## Engine invariants
- Keep `src/decision/engine.ts` a single self-contained runtime file (types via `import type` from `engine.types.ts`) so `npm run test:rules` runs under `node --experimental-strip-types` with no build step.
- Never regress the engine: `npm run test:rules` must stay green and `npm run typecheck` must not add errors (one pre-existing error in `src/components/app-tabs.web.tsx` is unrelated).
- The 26 CWCS dressing strings are transcribed from a PDF image — verify against the source before graded use.

## Frontier models
- Route VLM + LLM through **Vercel AI Gateway** (AI SDK `ai@^6`, `provider/model` strings, OIDC auth). Resolve model IDs via `getAvailableModels()`; don't hardcode. SAM 2 is NOT on the gateway — separate GPU endpoint (Replicate/Modal).

## Expo
- Expo SDK 57 — read https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v57.0.0/ before writing Expo code (see `AGENTS.md`).
